# Tendril monorepo — "Tendril android", "Tendril windows" and "shared" in one tree.
# `shared` stays a sibling of its consumers, never nested under them (spec §11/§12.5):
# both settings.gradle.kts files resolve it as includeBuild("../shared"), so one clone
# has to reproduce that arrangement exactly.

# --- Signing material. -----------------------------------------------------------
# Release keys never go in here.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pepk

# ...with one deliberate exception. The shared debug keystore is committed on
# purpose, which is what its name is for: every machine then signs debug builds
# with the same key, so moving between them doesn't force an uninstall on a
# signature mismatch. app/build.gradle.kts hard-references it, so without it a
# fresh clone cannot assemble a debug build at all.
# Alias androiddebugkey, password "android" — both public by definition, and a
# debug key cannot sign for Play. This exemption must never be widened.
!Tendril android/keystores/my-shared-debug.keystore

# --- Machine-specific -----------------------------------------------------------
# local.properties pins sdk.dir to an absolute path on one machine; the file even
# says so. Not portable, not shared.
local.properties
*.local.properties

# --- Gradle and build output ----------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
captures/
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/
*.hprof

# JVM crash debris. The Kotlin/Gradle daemon drops these next to the build it died
# in — 9 MB of them were sitting in shared/ and Tendril android/ already.
replay_pid*.log
hs_err_pid*.log
core.*

# Wrapper jar is intentionally NOT ignored: it is what makes ./gradlew work on a
# fresh clone.

# --- IDE ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.kotlin/

# --- Local agent/tool state -----------------------------------------------------
.claude/

# --- OS -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
